From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pymnn: do not hardcode manylinux1_x86_64 as the wheel
 plat-name on Linux

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 is unlisted by upstream's own packaging script]

build_wheel.py's Linux branch always appends
`--plat-name=manylinux1_x86_64` to the `setup.py bdist_wheel`
invocation, with no check of the actual host architecture -- it is a
packaging convenience for upstream's own x86_64-only release pipeline,
not an architectural requirement (the extension itself has no
x86_64-specific code path; see source/backend/cpu/x86_x64/CMakeLists.txt's
own CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR gating). Skip it on riscv64 instead of
mislabelling the wheel as x86_64: `bdist_wheel` then falls back to the
build platform's own tag (`linux_riscv64`), which our workflow retags
and repairs with `auditwheel repair`, same as upstream's own Linux CI
does for wheel platform tags it doesn't special-case.

diff --git a/pymnn/pip_package/build_wheel.py b/pymnn/pip_package/build_wheel.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/pymnn/pip_package/build_wheel.py
+++ b/pymnn/pip_package/build_wheel.py
@@ -26,7 +26,8 @@ if __name__ == '__main__':
         shutil.rmtree('build')
     comm_args = '--version ' + args.version
     if IS_LINUX:
-        comm_args += ' --plat-name=manylinux1_x86_64'
+        if platform.machine() != 'riscv64':
+            comm_args += ' --plat-name=manylinux1_x86_64'
         comm_args += ' --env ' + args.env  if args.env else ''
         comm_args += ' --serving' if args.serving else ''
     if IS_WINDOWS:
--
